@startuml
title Stays4Pilgrims - Media upload, contribution and moderation communication
scale 0.95
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam maxMessageSize 52
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantPadding 12
  BoxPadding 10
  MessageAlign center
  ArrowThickness 1
}

actor User
participant "Stays4Pilgrims Frontend" as FE
participant "Backend API" as API
participant "Upload Service" as UploadSvc
participant "Moderation Service" as ModSvc
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Cloudinary" as Cloudinary
participant "Email Service" as Email

group 1) Media upload
  User -> FE : Select image/file
  FE -> API : POST /upload
  API -> UploadSvc : validate and process upload
  UploadSvc -> Cloudinary : store file
  Cloudinary --> UploadSvc : public URL
  UploadSvc --> API : media metadata
  API --> FE : upload response
end

group 2) Content contribution
  alt Avatar
    FE -> API : POST /accounts/update
    API -> DB : update user avatar
    API --> FE : account updated
  else Accommodation photo
    FE -> API : POST /Accommodations/handle {action:addphotos}
    API -> ModSvc : create moderation item
    ModSvc -> DB : state = pending
    ModSvc -> Email : notify admins
    API --> FE : contribution accepted
  end
end

group 3) Moderation queue
  FE -> API : comments / edit requests
  API -> ModSvc : validate and enqueue
  ModSvc -> DB : save pending request
  ModSvc -> Email : notify moderators
  API --> FE : pending status
end

group 4) Review and decision
  User -> FE : Admin opens moderation queue
  FE -> API : list pending items
  API -> DB : load pending items
  API --> FE : pending list
  FE -> API : approve or reject
  API -> ModSvc : apply decision
  ModSvc -> DB : update final state
end

group 5) User notification
  ModSvc -> Email : send decision result
  API --> FE : moderation result
  FE --> User : final feedback
end

note over FE,API
Communication diagram at macro level.
Technical details in:
- sequence-upload-moderation
- sequence-add-comment
- sequence-add-accommodation
end note

@enduml
